Chapter: Armor1998

 The June 1998 armor defence (draxinar's OUO, a C translation of the 1998 UoDemo.exe server; combat.c and weapon.c).
 A landed melee blow (Combat_CalcArmorAbsorption, 0x004452D8) picks one of 14 armor groups at random, takes the worn
 piece with the highest rating among the group's layers (CMobile_GetBestArmorInGroup, 0x00444434, armorGroupTable
 0x00614FC0), and that piece absorbs a random amount from rating / 4 to (rating + 1) / 2 of the damage, never more than
 the damage (Combat_ApplyDurabilityLoss, 0x00444C75, damage type 1). A piece's rating is its armor class scaled by its
 wear, floor((hits / max hits + 1.5) / 2 * AC) (CItem_GetArmorRating 0x004DF86D, CItem_CalcAC_Inner 0x004DFAE8).
 Armor classes are rundir weapons/stats "Armor Class" matched by name to the 1.25 TILEDATA.MUL art names; where rundir
 defines a name twice the first definition is taken (as SmithModel takes Heater Shield 144); hats are rundir's "Hat"
 (weapon.300), boots its Knee Boots, a shirt its Long Sleeved Shirt, long pants its Trousers, a robe weapon.338.

  a98-ac : Integer -> Integer
  a98-ac (g) =
    if g == #1408 | g == #1409 | g == #140A | g == #140B | g == #140E | g == #140F | g == #1410 | g == #1411
      | g == #1412 | g == #1413 | g == #1414 | g == #1415 | g == #1416 | g == #1417 | g == #1418 | g == #1419
      | g == #141A | g == #144E | g == #144F | g == #1450 | g == #1451 | g == #1452 | g == #1453 | g == #1454
      | g == #1455 | g == #1456 | g == #1457 | g == #1C04 | g == #1C05 then 30
    else if g == #13BB | g == #13BC | g == #13BD | g == #13BE | g == #13BF | g == #13C0 | g == #13C1 | g == #13C2
      | g == #13C3 | g == #13C4 then 23
    else if g == #13E5 | g == #13E6 | g == #13E7 | g == #13E8 | g == #13E9 | g == #13EA | g == #13EB | g == #13EC
      | g == #13ED | g == #13EE | g == #13EF | g == #13F0 | g == #13F1 | g == #13F2 | g == #1F0B | g == #1F0C then 20
    else if g == #140C | g == #140D then 18
    else if g == #13D4 | g == #13D5 | g == #13D6 | g == #13D7 | g == #13D8 | g == #13D9 | g == #13DA | g == #13DB
      | g == #13DC | g == #13DD | g == #13DE | g == #13DF | g == #13E0 | g == #13E1 | g == #13E2 | g == #1C02
      | g == #1C03 | g == #1C0C | g == #1C0D then 16
    else if g == #1F03 | g == #1F04 then 15
    else if g == #13C5 | g == #13C6 | g == #13C7 | g == #13C8 | g == #13C9 | g == #13CA | g == #13CB | g == #13CC
      | g == #13CD | g == #13CE | g == #13CF | g == #13D0 | g == #13D1 | g == #13D2 | g == #13D3 | g == #1C00
      | g == #1C01 | g == #1C06 | g == #1C07 | g == #1C08 | g == #1C09 | g == #1C0A | g == #1C0B | g == #1DB9
      | g == #1DBA then 13
    else if g == #170B | g == #170C then 7
    else if g == #1545 | g == #1546 | g == #1547 | g == #1548 | g == #1711 | g == #1712 then 6
    else if g == #141B | g == #141C | g == #1515 | g == #1530 | g == #1549 | g == #154A | g == #154B | g == #154C
      | g == #1EFF | g == #1F00 | g == #1F01 | g == #1F02 then 5
    else if g == #1516 | g == #1517 | g == #1518 | g == #1531 then 4
    else if g == #152E | g == #152F | g == #1537 | g == #1538 | g == #1539 | g == #153A | g == #170D | g == #170E
      | g == #170F | g == #1710 | g == #1713 | g == #1714 | g == #1715 | g == #1716 | g == #1717 | g == #1718
      | g == #1719 | g == #171A | g == #171B | g == #171C | g == #172E then 3
    else if g == #153F | g == #1540 | g == #1543 | g == #1544 then 1
    else 0

 armorGroupTable: 14 groups of up to 4 layers (0 ends a group): helm, helm, neck, five chest groups (chest, shirt, robe,
 cloak), three leg groups (leggings, pants, shoes, skirt), two arm groups (arms, shirt), hands.
  a98-groups : List Integer = [6, 0, 0, 0, 6, 0, 0, 0, 10, 0, 0, 0, 13, 5, 22, 20, 13, 5, 22, 20, 13, 5, 22, 20,
    13, 5, 22, 20, 13, 5, 22, 20, 24, 4, 3, 23, 24, 4, 3, 23, 24, 4, 3, 23, 19, 5, 0, 0, 19, 5, 0, 0, 7, 0, 0, 0]
  a98-group-count : Integer = 14
  a98-layer : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  a98-layer (group) (j) = if group < 0 | group >= a98-group-count | j < 0 | j > 3 then 0 else list-at a98-groups (group * 4 + j)
 A piece's rating from its armor class, hits and max hits, after the smith band (per mille, Smith1998 x1.2 and x0.8
 on the class). UOAIX keeps no hits for clothing (DurabilityData has no range for it), so a max of 0 rates as whole.
  a98-rating : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  a98-rating (ac) (hits) (top) (band) = let base = ac * band / 1000
    in if base <= 0 then 0 else if top <= 0 then base * 5 / 4 else (2 * max 0 hits + 3 * top) * base / (4 * top)
 GetRandomRange(rating / 4, (rating + 1) / 2) from a non-negative roll.
  a98-absorb : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  a98-absorb (rating) (roll) = if rating <= 0 then 0
    else let lo = rating / 4 in let hi = (rating + 1) / 2 in lo + int-mod roll (hi - lo + 1)
  a98-reduce : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  a98-reduce (damage) (absorbed) = if absorbed >= damage then 0 else damage - absorbed